{
  "$comment": "Relay multi-key storage and binding. Connection-level `relayKeys` is an ordered list of {id, name?, apiKey, status?}; the first entry is the primary key and its secret is always `provider.apiKey` (its own `apiKey` slot is ignored and stored empty). Absent list = one implicit key {id: implicitKeyID} whose secret is provider.apiKey: legacy single-key connections need no migration. The list is written only by user key operations and, on a single-key connection, by the first key-status write, which stores a one-entry list [{id: implicitKeyID, apiKey: \"\", status}]; enabling, binding and catalog listing still write nothing for one key. Model-level local-only fields: `relayKeyID` (explicit binding; absent or dangling = primary), `relayListedByKeyIDs` (catalog entries only; key ids in key order that listed the model; absent = listed by the primary), `relayDeniedKeyID` (the key that got a model_access_denied, key-access.v1.json; shown only while it equals the model's effective key). Family for binding = cached Server model-facts by-model family, else the existing RelayFamilyHeuristics (family-fixtures.json); the fixture injects `families` directly. Test names: KEY-BIND-<caseId>, KEY-CATALOG-<caseId>, KEY-OPS-<caseId>, KEY-READ-<caseId>, KEY-LEGACY-<caseId>, KEY-SHELL-<caseId>.",
  "version": 1,
  "implicitKeyID": "initial",
  "keyStatusStates": ["ok", "invalid", "denied", "limited", "failed"],
  "bindCases": {
    "$comment": "bind(keys, catalog, enabled, targetModelID, family) -> keyID | null. keys = ordered key ids. Rules in order: (0) one key or none -> null (nothing is written); (1) exactly one key lists the target -> that key; (2) several keys list it -> the effective key of the first enabled model (enabled order) of the same family whose effective key is among the listing keys, else the first listing key in KEY order; (3) no key lists it (manual id) -> same-family enabled model's effective key, else the primary (keys[0]). Effective key of an enabled model = its relayKeyID when that id is in keys, else keys[0]. Catalog entries without relayListedByKeyIDs count as listed by keys[0]. Family null never matches.",
    "cases": [
      { "caseId": "single_key_writes_nothing", "keys": ["initial"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "enabled": [], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai" }, "expect": null },
      { "caseId": "only_one_key_lists_target", "keys": ["initial", "k-claude"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "enabled": [], "target": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "families": { "claude-sonnet-4-5": "anthropic" }, "expect": "k-claude" },
      { "caseId": "several_keys_follow_enabled_same_family", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "gpt-4.1", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai", "gpt-4.1": "openai" }, "expect": "k-b" },
      { "caseId": "several_keys_no_family_enabled_first_in_key_order", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b", "initial"] }], "enabled": [], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai" }, "expect": "initial" },
      { "caseId": "family_key_not_listing_target_is_ignored", "keys": ["initial", "k-b", "k-c"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b", "k-c"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "gpt-4.1", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai", "gpt-4.1": "openai" }, "expect": "k-b" },
      { "caseId": "other_family_enabled_is_ignored", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai", "claude-opus-4": "anthropic" }, "expect": "initial" },
      { "caseId": "manual_id_follows_same_family", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "target": "claude-private-1", "families": { "claude-private-1": "anthropic", "claude-opus-4": "anthropic" }, "expect": "k-b" },
      { "caseId": "manual_id_no_family_uses_primary", "keys": ["k-b", "initial"], "catalog": [], "enabled": [], "target": "my-model", "families": { "my-model": null }, "expect": "k-b" },
      { "caseId": "enabled_without_key_id_counts_as_primary", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "gpt-4.1" }], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai", "gpt-4.1": "openai" }, "expect": "initial" },
      { "caseId": "enabled_dangling_key_id_counts_as_primary", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "gpt-4.1", "relayKeyID": "k-deleted" }], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai", "gpt-4.1": "openai" }, "expect": "initial" },
      { "caseId": "unknown_target_family_never_matches", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "mystery", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b", "initial"] }], "enabled": [{ "id": "other", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "target": "mystery", "families": { "mystery": null, "other": null }, "expect": "initial" },
      { "caseId": "legacy_catalog_entry_counts_as_primary_listing", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "enabled": [], "target": "gpt-4o", "families": { "gpt-4o": "openai" }, "expect": "initial" }
    ]
  },
  "catalogCases": {
    "$comment": "merge(keys, previousCatalog, results) -> {catalog, statuses}; used only when the connection has 2+ keys (one key keeps the existing single-key refresh path byte for byte). results[keyID] is {ok:[ids in upstream order]} | {status:<int|null>, body:<string>} (failure; null = network / decode) | \"skipped\" (not fetched this time, e.g. only another key was replaced). Order: walk keys in key order; an ok key contributes its fetched ids in upstream order, a failed or skipped key contributes the previous catalog entries that listed it, in previous order; first occurrence wins. relayListedByKeyIDs = every key (key order) that lists the id: ok keys by their fetched list, failed / skipped keys by the previous listing. An id listed by no key leaves the catalog (enabled and manual models are kept by the existing retention, not by this function). Status: ok -> ok; failed -> key-access classify: key_invalid -> invalid, key_limited -> limited, else 403 -> denied, else failed; skipped -> unchanged (absent in expect). A failure never clears what that key listed before.",
    "cases": [
      { "caseId": "union_in_key_order", "keys": ["initial", "k-claude"], "previous": [], "results": { "initial": { "ok": ["gpt-4o", "gpt-4.1"] }, "k-claude": { "ok": ["claude-sonnet-4-5", "gpt-4o"] } }, "expect": { "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-claude"] }, { "id": "gpt-4.1", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "statuses": { "initial": "ok", "k-claude": "ok" } } },
      { "caseId": "failed_key_keeps_previous_listing", "keys": ["initial", "k-claude"], "previous": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "results": { "initial": { "ok": ["gpt-4o"] }, "k-claude": { "status": 401, "body": "{\"error\":\"Invalid API key\"}" } }, "expect": { "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "statuses": { "initial": "ok", "k-claude": "invalid" } } },
      { "caseId": "all_failed_keeps_everything", "keys": ["initial", "k-claude"], "previous": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "results": { "initial": { "status": null, "body": "" }, "k-claude": { "status": 503, "body": "busy" } }, "expect": { "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-claude"] }], "statuses": { "initial": "failed", "k-claude": "failed" } } },
      { "caseId": "dropped_by_its_only_key_leaves", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "previous": [{ "id": "old-model", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }, { "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }], "results": { "initial": { "ok": ["gpt-4o"] }, "k-b": { "ok": ["new-model"] } }, "expect": { "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "new-model", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }], "statuses": { "initial": "ok", "k-b": "ok" } } },
      { "caseId": "skipped_key_keeps_listing_and_status", "keys": ["initial", "k-b"], "previous": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }, { "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }], "results": { "initial": { "ok": ["gpt-4.1"] }, "k-b": "skipped" }, "expect": { "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4.1", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }, { "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }, { "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }], "statuses": { "initial": "ok" } } },
      { "caseId": "status_mapping_403_quota_and_plain", "keys": ["initial", "k-b", "k-c"], "previous": [], "results": { "initial": { "status": 403, "body": "{\"code\":\"INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE\",\"message\":\"Insufficient balance\"}" }, "k-b": { "status": 403, "body": "Forbidden" }, "k-c": { "status": 429, "body": "" } }, "expect": { "catalog": [], "statuses": { "initial": "limited", "k-b": "denied", "k-c": "limited" } } }
    ]
  },
  "opsCases": {
    "$comment": "Pure key operations on a provider (no network; refetching belongs to the refresh path: after add every key is refetched, after replaceSecret only that key with the others `skipped`; a replaced key's status is cleared on a one-entry list exactly as on a longer one). provider = {apiKey, relayKeys?, models:[{id, relayKeyID?, relayDeniedKeyID?, relayTransport?, relayTransportSource?}], catalog:[{id, relayListedByKeyIDs?}]}. Invariant after every op: relayKeys[0].apiKey is stored empty and provider.apiKey is the primary secret. Once a connection has 2+ keys every enabled model carries an explicit relayKeyID, so reordering never silently moves a model to another key. Refused (nothing written, same refusal value everywhere): add with an empty or existing id; replaceSecret / delete / rename with an unknown id; delete of the last key; move to an index outside the list; rebind to an unknown key or of a model that is not enabled; and every rename / move / rebind on a connection without relayKeys.",
    "cases": [
      { "caseId": "add_key_materializes_list_and_pins_models", "op": { "type": "add", "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }] } },
      { "caseId": "rename_key", "op": { "type": "rename", "id": "k-b", "name": "Anthropic" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [], "catalog": [] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Anthropic", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "replace_secret_clears_status_and_denial_keeps_catalog", "op": { "type": "replaceSecret", "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b2" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b", "status": { "state": "invalid", "httpStatus": 401 } }], "models": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b", "relayDeniedKeyID": "k-b" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b2" }], "models": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }] } },
      { "caseId": "replace_primary_secret_writes_api_key", "op": { "type": "replaceSecret", "id": "initial", "apiKey": "sk-a2" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [], "catalog": [] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a2", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "reorder_moves_primary_secret", "op": { "type": "move", "id": "k-b", "toIndex": 0 }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-b", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "initial", "apiKey": "sk-a" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "delete_key_rebinds_to_primary_and_prunes_catalog", "op": { "type": "delete", "id": "k-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }, { "id": "k-c", "apiKey": "sk-c" }], "models": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b", "relayDeniedKeyID": "k-b" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }, { "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-c", "apiKey": "sk-c" }], "models": [{ "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }] } },
      { "caseId": "delete_primary_promotes_next", "op": { "type": "delete", "id": "initial" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-b", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "delete_last_key_is_refused", "op": { "type": "delete", "id": "initial" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "rebind_clears_denial_and_reachable_transport", "op": { "type": "rebind", "modelID": "gpt-4o", "keyID": "k-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial", "relayDeniedKeyID": "initial", "relayTransport": "openai_chat_completions", "relayTransportSource": "reachable" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "k-b" }], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "rebind_keeps_user_transport", "op": { "type": "rebind", "modelID": "gpt-4o", "keyID": "k-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial", "relayTransport": "anthropic_messages", "relayTransportSource": "user" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "k-b", "relayTransport": "anthropic_messages", "relayTransportSource": "user" }], "catalog": [] } },
      { "caseId": "add_to_single_entry_list_keeps_primary_status", "op": { "type": "add", "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "ok", "httpStatus": 200 } }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "ok", "httpStatus": 200 } }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial"] }] } },
      { "caseId": "replace_secret_single_entry_list_clears_status", "op": { "type": "replaceSecret", "id": "initial", "apiKey": "sk-a2" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "invalid", "httpStatus": 401 } }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "expect": { "apiKey": "sk-a2", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] } },
      { "caseId": "add_empty_id_is_refused", "op": { "type": "add", "id": "", "name": "X", "apiKey": "sk-x" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "add_duplicate_id_is_refused", "op": { "type": "add", "id": "k-b", "name": "X", "apiKey": "sk-x" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "rename_unknown_id_is_refused", "op": { "type": "rename", "id": "k-zzz", "name": "X" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "replace_unknown_id_is_refused", "op": { "type": "replaceSecret", "id": "k-zzz", "apiKey": "sk-x" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "delete_unknown_id_is_refused", "op": { "type": "delete", "id": "k-zzz" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "move_out_of_range_is_refused", "op": { "type": "move", "id": "k-b", "toIndex": 2 }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "rebind_unknown_key_is_refused", "op": { "type": "rebind", "modelID": "gpt-4o", "keyID": "k-zzz" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "rebind_model_not_enabled_is_refused", "op": { "type": "rebind", "modelID": "not-enabled", "keyID": "k-b" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "" }, { "id": "k-b", "apiKey": "sk-b" }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "implicit_rename_is_refused", "op": { "type": "rename", "id": "initial", "name": "X" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "implicit_move_is_refused", "op": { "type": "move", "id": "initial", "toIndex": 0 }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" },
      { "caseId": "implicit_rebind_is_refused", "op": { "type": "rebind", "modelID": "gpt-4o", "keyID": "initial" }, "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [] }, "expect": "refused" }
    ]
  },
  "readCases": {
    "$comment": "Read model for the model library (no UI here). rows(provider) -> per key in key order {id, name, isPrimary, status (state, or null = never checked, which renders no status word and no mark), catalogCount (catalog entries listing it), enabledCount (enabled models whose effective key is it)}; showsKeyUI = 2+ keys; per enabled model: boundKeyID (effective key), alternateKeyIDs (other keys listing it in the catalog, key order), deniedOnCurrentKey (relayDeniedKeyID == boundKeyID). Masked secrets use each end's existing apiKey preview helper and are not compared here.",
    "cases": [
      { "caseId": "single_entry_list_with_status", "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "ok", "httpStatus": 200 } }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "expect": { "showsKeyUI": false, "rows": [{ "id": "initial", "name": null, "isPrimary": true, "status": "ok", "catalogCount": 1, "enabledCount": 1 }], "models": { "gpt-4o": { "boundKeyID": "initial", "alternateKeyIDs": [], "deniedOnCurrentKey": false } } } },
      { "caseId": "legacy_single_key", "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }, { "id": "gpt-4.1" }] }, "expect": { "showsKeyUI": false, "rows": [{ "id": "initial", "name": null, "isPrimary": true, "status": null, "catalogCount": 2, "enabledCount": 1 }], "models": { "gpt-4o": { "boundKeyID": "initial", "alternateKeyIDs": [], "deniedOnCurrentKey": false } } } },
      { "caseId": "two_keys_with_denial", "provider": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "name": "OpenAI", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "ok", "httpStatus": 200 } }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "apiKey": "sk-b", "status": { "state": "invalid", "httpStatus": 401 } }], "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayKeyID": "initial", "relayDeniedKeyID": "initial" }, { "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayKeyID": "k-b", "relayDeniedKeyID": "initial" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["initial", "k-b"] }, { "id": "claude-opus-4", "relayListedByKeyIDs": ["k-b"] }] }, "expect": { "showsKeyUI": true, "rows": [{ "id": "initial", "name": "OpenAI", "isPrimary": true, "status": "ok", "catalogCount": 1, "enabledCount": 1 }, { "id": "k-b", "name": "Claude", "isPrimary": false, "status": "invalid", "catalogCount": 2, "enabledCount": 1 }], "models": { "gpt-4o": { "boundKeyID": "initial", "alternateKeyIDs": ["k-b"], "deniedOnCurrentKey": true }, "claude-opus-4": { "boundKeyID": "k-b", "alternateKeyIDs": [], "deniedOnCurrentKey": false } } } }
    ]
  },
  "legacyCases": {
    "$comment": "Zero migration: a stored single-key relay provider from before multi-key support (no relayKeys, no model key fields) decodes and behaves exactly as before, and multi-key code paths write none of the new fields for it, except the key status: a catalog refresh (or any real request, key-access.v1.json) records the primary's status as a one-entry relayKeys list. `relayKeys` in expect compares id, apiKey and status.state / status.httpStatus when given (checkedAt is not compared). Refresh results: {ok:[ids]} or {status, body} (failure: catalog keeps what it had). Each end runs these through its production decode + the production enable / catalog-refresh merge path, not through hand-built objects.",
    "cases": [
      { "caseId": "decode_has_one_implicit_key", "stored": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "expect": { "keyIDs": ["initial"], "resolve": { "gpt-4o": "sk-a", "null": "sk-a" } } },
      { "caseId": "enable_writes_no_key_id", "stored": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }, { "id": "gpt-4.1" }] }, "enable": "gpt-4.1", "expect": { "relayKeysPersisted": false, "modelKeyFieldsPersisted": false } },
      { "caseId": "catalog_refresh_writes_no_listing", "stored": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "refresh": { "ok": ["gpt-4o", "gpt-4.1"] }, "expect": { "relayKeysPersisted": true, "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "ok" } }], "modelKeyFieldsPersisted": false, "catalogIDs": ["gpt-4o", "gpt-4.1"] } },
      { "caseId": "catalog_refresh_failure_writes_status_only", "stored": { "apiKey": "sk-a", "models": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }], "catalog": [{ "id": "gpt-4o" }] }, "refresh": { "status": 401, "body": "{\"error\":{\"message\":\"Invalid API key\"}}" }, "expect": { "relayKeysPersisted": true, "relayKeys": [{ "id": "initial", "apiKey": "", "status": { "state": "invalid", "httpStatus": 401 } }], "modelKeyFieldsPersisted": false, "catalogIDs": ["gpt-4o"] } }
    ]
  },
  "shellCases": {
    "$comment": "The catalog response decoder of the production refresh path accepts the three upstream shells and yields the same ids in order.",
